cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Arwad: R, compiled"
abstract: "Arwad is a statistical programming language that keeps R's syntax and package ecosystem and compiles numerical work to native code through the Goose systems language, with deterministic, garbage-collection-free memory and results equivalent to GNU R. Version 0.1.0 is the arwad R package: aw_compile() compiles R functions written in a statistical subset to native code, bit-identical to GNU R across a 201-function corpus on Linux, macOS and Windows; compiled statistical engines bootstrap least-squares and generalised linear models with R's own results and PLS-SEM models with the results of the seminr package; and aw_pls_ci() gives the bias-corrected percentile confidence intervals recommended for PLS-SEM."
